    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d743">

                <pb facs="0695" n="683" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg683"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.51/67: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Saudi Arabia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Moose</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jidda</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-13T08:00:00+03:06">April 13, 1944—8
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>106. My 96, April 8, 9 a.m.<anchor n="62" xml:id="d743-f1"/> Both Saudi Finance
                    Minister and Acting Foreign Minister state that Saudi Government must have
                    assistance in excess of that contemplated in budget figures of British
                    Minister.</p>
                <p>They have indicated that they would like the United States to supply deficiency.
                    Request for specific sums expected in few days.</p>
                <p>Sent Department, code text airmail to Cairo for Landis.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moose</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
